# The integration cochain defines a linear cohomology map

Theorem statement: `MTT.Cohomology.integration_linear_map_exists`
(`f7ad6366-1756-4782-823a-612563ccc48c`), by davidloeffler, 2026-09-06.

Proof: submission `9672543a-2d93-458b-b602-0edeaa760728`, by cbirkbeck, 2026-09-06 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

Let $N>0$ and $k\ge 2$. For a weight-$k$ cusp form $f$ on $\Gamma_1(N)$, let $\Phi_f$ be the
polynomial-valued cusp-to-cusp integration cochain

$$
\Phi_f(x,y)=-2\pi i\int_y^x f(z)(zX+Y)^{k-2}\,dz.
$$

Then $\Phi_f$ is homogeneous of degree $k-2$, satisfies the modular-symbol cocycle relation, and is
$\Gamma_1(N)$-equivariant. Moreover, the assignment $f\mapsto\Phi_f$ defines a complex-linear map
from cusp forms to $H_c(N,k-2;\mathbf C)$.

**Formalization Note** The asserted map is required to have underlying function exactly
`integrationCochain f`, so the theorem includes both well-definedness in the compactly supported
cohomology model and linearity.

## Explanation of the source proof

We reduce the existence of the integration map to the sibling `cuspPrimitive_analytic_relations`
(the $\Gamma_1(N)$-equivariance, additivity and homogeneity of the cusp primitive $P_f$), which is
the assumption of this submission; the rest is bookkeeping.

The integration cochain $\Phi_f(x,y)=P_f(y)-P_f(x)$ lies in
$H_c=\operatorname{Hom}_{\Gamma_1(N)}(\operatorname{Div}^0,\operatorname{Sym}^{k-2})$ (the mission's
`compactSupport`): its values are homogeneous of degree $k-2$ because $P_f(r)$ is a sum of monomials
$X^jY^{k-2-j}$ with $j\le k-2$ and $P_f(\infty)=0$ (`cuspPrimitive_mem_Sym`); the cocycle relation
$\Phi_f(x,y)+\Phi_f(y,z)=\Phi_f(x,z)$ is telescoping; and for $\gamma\in\Gamma_1(N)$ the
equivariance $P_f(\gamma x)=\gamma\cdot P_f(x)+P_f(\gamma\infty)$ gives $\Phi_f(\gamma x,\gamma
y)=\gamma\cdot P_f(y)-\gamma\cdot P_f(x)=\gamma\cdot\Phi_f(x,y)$, the constant $P_f(\gamma\infty)$
cancelling.

The map $f\mapsto\Phi_f$ is $\mathbf C$-linear because $P_{f+g}=P_f+P_g$ and $P_{af}=aP_f$ pointwise
on cusps; packaging it as a `LinearMap` into `Hc` gives the required $I$ with $(If)$ equal to the
integration cochain by construction.

